│ patch_description        │ Inspired by the original ansatz’s strengths (simple single-qubit rotations plus a fixed   │
│                          │ entangling CZ backbone with a final phase layer), but redesigned to be fundamentally more │
│                          │ parameter-efficient.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key novelty:                                                                              │
│                          │ - **Radically reduced parameter count via sharing:** instead of independent parameters    │
│                          │ for all 8 qubits (24 params/block in the seed), this block uses **parity + half-qubit     │
│                          │ sharing** (only 4 “pre” rotation params, 2 parameterized controlled-rotation params, and  │
│                          │ 2 “post” params → 8 unique params/block).                                                 │
│                          │ - **Task-aligned inductive bias:** keeps a **CZ entangling ring/tessellation structure**  │
│                          │ so the fixed feature-map couplings can propagate globally, while adding only a couple of  │
│                          │ **parameterized CRZ “long-range” links** to increase expressivity without parameter       │
│                          │ explosion.                                                                                │
│                          │ - **Preserves the fixed training loop and feature map contract**, including re-uploading  │
│                          │ (l=3) and block repetition (p=2), by only editing `ANSATZ_SPEC`.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve the combined score mainly through better **parameter efficiency**     │
│                          │ (far fewer trainable circuit parameters) while maintaining high representational          │
│                          │ capacity.                                                                                 │
