│                          │ - It uses independent rotation parameters for every qubit in the RY and RZ layers to      │
│                          │ allow for local subspace customization.                                                   │
│                          │ - It employs a "checkerboard" of CZ gates, which ensures that all qubits are entangled    │
│                          │ efficiently, propagating information globally through the circuit.                        │
│                          │ - Finally, it incorporates a long-range CRZ layer, which provides parameterized,          │
│                          │ non-local phase correlation. This structure is more stable during gradient-based training │
│                          │ (via Adam) than the previous highly-redundant designs, leading to better convergence and  │
│                          │ reduced generalization error.                                                             │
